I'm going to point out only the pros and cons because i have people to send to the gulag and don't have the time to write a full review, yet.
Pros:
-Immersive realistic medieval world;
-Amazing combat system;
-Large map with a good instant map creator for battles;
-Excellent faction diplomacy mechanics (for an fps rpg);
-Large choice of weapons and armour, that  match existing kinds of armour that existed at the time.
-Ease to mod;
-Excellent mechanics for creating parties and armies, with realistic modifiers such as morale, salary, etc..;
-Massive battles up to 300 people at a time, with tons of bodies that stay;
-Amazing siege system with victory or defeat bringing criteria such as remaining food in the city/castle, how long to build siege equipment
-Doesn't require a powerfull computer;
-Tons of great mods available;
-No capitalist foreign intervention;
-Freedom of choice relative to your history, what you do, what you become, you can shape the fait of kingdoms, drive them to be empires or erase them from history, become a dreadfull bandit or a renown lord, you can even found your own kingdom;
-Good multiplayer includes servers with up to 200 slots, amazing maps and game modes, and tons of fun, especially in a clan;
Cons:
-Graphics;
-Game instability due to the insalation of mods or add-ons;
-Once you conquer Calradia there is not much else to do;
-Singleplayer will get you hooked up for 200 hours before you go buy Napoleonic Wars and forget about Native;
-Swadians knights=rage+frustration;
-"Overpowered" weapons in multiplayer don't allow for good balance in matches, especially sieges;
-Hard to learn combat since singleplayer bots play in a different style from 90% of players who won't give you a chance in the game and will constantly abuse you;
-No russian bias;
9.7/10 would m&b again.

